{%- comment -%}
  The season's recap reel, as a bar directly under that season's divider — so
  the reel sits at the head of the weeks it recaps instead of floating above an
  archive that spans two seasons.

  Two rows in one mat panel:
    1. the bar — season, dates, runtime, and the toggle. Click it and the reel
       drops in below. A <details> does that: same device as the hero's "About
       the club", no JS, keyboard-operable for free.
    2. the season's weeks as a row of Luma covers in polaroid frames, one per
       week, each linking to its page. The covers ARE the index — the same art
       the week's card carries below, so the row is recognisable rather than
       decorative, and the week number rides in the polaroid's chin where a
       print's label goes.

  Row 2 sits OUTSIDE the <summary> on purpose: a summary is one click target,
  and links nested inside it both follow and toggle. Outside it, the index stays
  usable whether the reel is open or shut.

  params: season (name — must match `season_recap.season` to render anything)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign recap = site.data.mln.season_recap -%}
{%- if recap and recap.season == include.season -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The season's range, read back out of `seasons:` rather than restated. Walking
    newest-first, the entry BEFORE the recap's season is the one that ended it,
    so by the time we match we are holding its start: the season covers
    [own start, next season's start). Nothing to keep in sync by hand.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign recap_from = '' -%}
  {%- assign recap_until = '9999-12-31' -%}
  {%- assign next_start = '9999-12-31' -%}
  {%- for s in site.data.mln.seasons -%}
    {%- if s.name == recap.season -%}
      {%- assign recap_from = s.start -%}
      {%- assign recap_until = next_start -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign next_start = s.start -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign in_season = site.data.mln.weeks | where_exp: 'w', 'w.date >= recap_from' -%}
  {%- assign in_season = in_season | where_exp: 'w', 'w.date < recap_until' | sort: 'date' -%}
  <li class="mln-reel-li">
    <div class="mln-reel">
      <details class="mln-reel-fold">
        <summary class="mln-reel-bar">
          <span class="mln-reel-meta">
            <span class="mln-reel-kicker">
              Season recap
              {%- if recap.length %}
                <span class="mln-reel-len">{{ recap.length }}</span>
              {%- endif %}
            </span>
            <span class="mln-reel-title">{{ recap.season }}</span>
            <span class="mln-reel-line">{{ recap.line }}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="mln-reel-cta">
            <span class="mln-reel-cta-open">watch the reel <span class="mln-arrow">↓</span></span>
            <span class="mln-reel-cta-close">close <span class="mln-arrow">↑</span></span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="mln-reel-body">
          {%- comment -%}
            preload="none" — 13 MB behind a closed bar. Nothing is fetched until
            the bar is opened, and then only the poster, which is the reel's own
            end card and already carries the season and the dates.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <figure class="mln-reel-frame">
            <video
              controls
              playsinline
              preload="none"
              width="810"
              height="1440"
              poster="{{ recap.poster | relative_url }}"
              aria-label="{{ recap.season }} recap reel — {{ recap.line }}"
            >
              <source src="{{ recap.video | relative_url }}" type="video/mp4">
            </video>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </details>
      {%- if in_season.size > 0 -%}
        <nav class="mln-reel-strip" aria-label="{{ recap.season }} — every week">
          {%- for w in in_season -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Same cover the week's card uses, off the same Luma CDN, asked for
              at 240px — these are thumbnails, not card art.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign tsrc = w.cover -%}
            {%- if w.cover contains 'images.lumacdn.com/' -%}
              {%- unless w.cover contains 'cdn-cgi/image' -%}
                {%- assign tsrc = w.cover
                  | replace: 'images.lumacdn.com/', 'images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,quality=75,width=240/'
                -%}
              {%- endunless -%}
            {%- elsif w.cover contains 'images.unsplash.com/' -%}
              {%- assign tsrc = w.cover | replace: 'w=1080', 'w=240' -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            <a
              class="mln-reel-pola"
              href="{{ '/mln/week-' | append: w.num | append: '/' | relative_url }}"
              aria-label="Week {{ w.num }} — {{ w.title }}"
            >
              <span class="mln-reel-pola-img">
                {%- if tsrc -%}
                  <img src="{{ tsrc }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="mln-reel-pola-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ w.num | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </li>
{%- endif -%}
